  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Entropy is the measure of disorderliness. It means as disorderliness increases entropy increases.</p><p>Melting of ice leads to the formation of liquid water where the particles are in random motion which leads to an increase in entropy.</p><p>Option (c) is the correct option as in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>,</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>ii</mi><mo>)</mo></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>iv</mi><mo>)</mo></math> the state changes towards more random state, thus entropy increases.</p>",
    "image": null
